      "weight": 0.9,
      "depends_on": [4]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "claim": "Assuming similar stopping forces (e.g., drag, braking), a larger change in momentum requires a longer time.",
      "evidence": "Rearranging $\\Delta t = \\Delta p / F_{avg}$, if $\\Delta p$ is larger and $F_{avg}$ is comparable, $\\Delta t$ is larger.",
